              "text": "mūla, mūlae — \"a she-mule\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mūla parva est sed fortis. The she-mule is small but strong."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First declension, feminine: mūla, mūlae f., the female of mūlus. Romans said a mule never foals, so cum mūla pepererit meant 'never'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mūla is the feminine of mūlus 'mule' (Lewis & Short). EtymDB traces mūlus to PIE mukslós."
            }
          ]
        },
